			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Replace hardcoded output event strings with typed SkyEvent constants\n\nReplace hardcoded \"sky://output/*\" string literals in ChannelContent.rs and ChannelLifecycle.rs with typed constants from CommonLibrary::IPC::SkyEvent:\n- sky://output/append → SkyEvent::OutputAppend\n- sky://output/replace → SkyEvent::OutputReplace\n- sky://output/clear → SkyEvent::OutputClear\n- sky://output/create → SkyEvent::OutputCreate\n- sky://output/dispose → SkyEvent::OutputDispose\n\nUsing the SkyEvent enum ensures consistency across the codebase and reduces the risk of typos in event names.",
			"SHA": "21fbdf32a02153ea3fc22be35d5c2ea876f14daa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:40:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 3 components\n\nSynchronize Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky submodules with modularization and observability improvements:\n\n- **Cocoon:** Add Wave 7 instrumentation to $deltaExtensions handler — log added/removed counts, registry size, activation events, and wall-clock duration per delta. Emit extended deltaExtensions event with registrySize and durationMs fields. Also fix ISerializationResult/IDeserializationResult interfaces for TypeScript's exactOptionalPropertyTypes.\n\n- **Mountain:** Split monolithic 167KB WindServiceHandlers.rs into domain modules (Commands, Configuration, Extensions, FileSystem, Model, NativeHost, Navigation, Output, Search, Storage, Terminal, UI, Utilities). Similarly refactor CocoonService/mod.rs from 2800-line monolithic to domain modules (Auth, Command, Debug, Extension, FileSystem, Initialization, Output, Provider, Save, SCM, Secret, Task, Terminal, TreeView, Window, Workspace).\n\n- **Sky:** Add ExtensionChangeSubscriber that listens to Mountain's sky://extensions/installed and sky://extensions/uninstalled events, forwarding to VS Code's ExtensionEnablementService. Enables live sidebar updates after VSIX install/uninstall without workbench reload. Uses Effect.runFork for fire-and-forget semantics.\n\nThis completes the K2/K3 milestone for live extension state synchronization between Mountain and Wind/Sky frontend.",
			"SHA": "2c6da4377c7715f2be9a57a0f5b6d0345cce4f79"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:24:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 4 components\n\nSynchronize Cocoon, Common, Mountain, and Wind submodules with the following changes:\n\n- **Cocoon:** Refactor Window service from monolithic file into 7 focused modules (TextDocument, QuickInput, FileDialogs, StatusBar, OutputChannel, WebviewPanel, Progress) with Window/Index.ts as composition point. Follows the same modularization pattern as previous Message and WorkspaceNamespace refactoring.\n\n- **Common:** Add `SkyEvent` enum registry for Mountain→Wind Tauri events (~100 events covering Configuration, Debug, Diagnostics, Dialog, Documents, Editor, Extensions, etc.). Uses `DefineSkyEvent!` macro producing wire strings via `AsStr()` and parsing via `FromStr()`. Also adds 3 legacy channels to Channel.rs that predate the `prefix:method` convention.\n\n- **Mountain:** Remove accidental zero-byte `.bak` backup file from Source/Track/Effect directory.\n\n- **Wind:** Add SkyEvent.ts as TypeScript mirror of Rust SkyEvent enum for compile-time validated Tauri event subscriptions. Extend Channel.ts with 3 legacy channels (MountainGetStatus, UserInterface.ShowOpenDialog, UserInterface.ShowSaveDialog). Add ExtensionChangeStream.ts merging install/uninstall event streams. Update all call sites to use typed registry constants.\n\nThis establishes a robust typed event-based IPC surface from Mountain to Wind, eliminating silent runtime failures from string typos in event URIs.",
			"SHA": "d7655e692e65aa841d42a4722d3df589717a35bb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:10:12Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 5 components\n\nSynchronize Cocoon, Common, Mountain, Sky, and Wind submodules with the following improvements:\n\n- Cocoon: Split monolithic Message.ts and WorkspaceNamespace.ts into modular directories with separate modules for Types, Constants, VSBuffer, Validation, Serialization, Batching, and domain-specific namespaces (Configuration, FileSystem, Providers, Window services)\n\n- Common: Add 9 new IPC channels to the Channel registry — QuickInput (showInputBox, showQuickPick), TextFile (read, write, save), and WorkingCopy (getAllDirty, getDirtyCount, isDirty, setDirty) — completing the IPC contract for text editor and quick input services\n\n- Mountain: Add WindServiceHandlers for IPC bridge and CreateEffectForRequest effect creators across 20+ domain modules (Authentication, Clipboard, Commands, Configuration, Diagnostics, Documents, FileSystem, Git, Keybinding, Languages, NativeHost, SCM, Search, Secrets, StatusBar, Storage, Task, Terminal, TreeView, UserInterface, Webview, WindowUI, Workspace)\n\n- Sky: Minor dependency bumps (pnpm/action-setup 6.0.1→6.0.3, @xterm/xterm 6.1.0-beta.197→6.1.0-beta.199)\n\n- Wind: Migrate all 19 service Live layers to use typed Channel registry imports instead of free-text string literals, ensuring compile-time validation. Also extend Channel.ts with new channels for TextFile, WorkingCopy, and QuickInput.\n\nThese changes establish a robust typed IPC surface between Wind frontend and Mountain backend, completing the migration to compile-time validated channel references across all service layers.",
			"SHA": "a763530b40789b14eb250d9cd01ac4ba422e08c2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T23:43:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 4 components\n\nSynchronize Common, Mountain, Sky, and Wind submodules with the following changes:\n\n**Features:**\n- Sky: Add LAND_ENABLE_WIND to conditionally skip Wind bootstrap (Atom N2) — introduces environment variable that enables \"Mountain + bare workbench\" integration tests when set to \"false\" at build time. Vite inlines the comparison for tree-shaking, producing the smallest shippable surface where gRPC/Tauri IPC isn't desired. Mirrored into Vite's define config with default \"true\".\n- Wind: Add InstallVsix and Uninstall to ExtensionsService (Atom K5) — implement the contract with methods that accept .vsix path/file:// URI for installation, returning the ILocalExtension envelope from Mountain. Uninstall resolves with true after Mountain removes the install directory and broadcasts the uninstalled event. Refactor all IPC invokes to use the Channel registry instead of free-text string literals for compile-time validation. Prior implementation was a no-op stub returning null.\n\n**Updates:**\n- Common: Minor update\n- Mountain: Minor update\n\nThese changes deliver conditional Wind bootstrapping for minimal builds and enable functional VSIX extension management in the editor.",
			"SHA": "2ab3a64ceb14da69d1557cea9ce17c9c56416411"
		}
	],
